-Treatment descriptions:
+Treatment semantics:
 
-- No position encoding is the control and gives the transformer only causal order.
-- ALiBi adds head-specific linear attention biases without learned position tables.
-- Learned-position treatments add forward, reverse, or both learned index embeddings.
-- RoPE treatments rotate queries and keys with forward or reverse sequence indices.
-- Combination treatments compose the named learned, rotary, and ALiBi mechanisms without changing the rest of the selected recipe.
+- Additive forward learned position is added to the item representation. In combined r4 additive treatments, the transformer input is exactly `item + forward_normal + reverse_zero`: the reverse table starts at zero, so initialization matches the forward-only control and the reverse table receives a first-step gradient.
+- Concat fusion revision 3 preserves the item residual and adds `gate_zero * variance_preserved(DenseNet([item; learned position(s)]))`. Combined r4 concat keeps those fusion semantics but zero-initializes the reverse table under a separate metadata revision; the gate moves before gradients can enter the DenseNet and position branch.
+- Reverse learned absolute positions anchor the last valid token at index zero. A constant sequence offset cancels from RoPE's relative phases, so reverse RoPE is instead a sign-reversed pairwise phase parameterization, not an absolute end anchor.
+- ALiBi applies the same head-specific monotone attention bias in every named ALiBi treatment.
 
-Implementation: [treatment grid](configs/variant.py), [position and RoPE modules](../../dcn/nn/transformer.py#L130-L227), [transformer wiring](../../dcn/config/networks.py#L181-L242), and [ALiBi](https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.12409)/[RoPE](https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.09864) papers. On GPU, ALiBi uses FlashAttention's built-in bias path by passing `alibi_slopes` directly to [`flash_attn_varlen_func`](../../dcn/nn/transformer.py#L394-L411); the CPU integration fallback does not reproduce its numerical bias.
+Implementation and evidence: [current treatment identities](analysis/rq7_reinvestigation_candidates.py), [generated report code](analysis/rq7_reinvestigation_report.py), [approved protocol](protocol/rq7_reinvestigation_plan.md), [eligible native-500M tuning ledger](scratchpad/rq7_reinvestigation_tuning_500m.md), and [machine-readable evidence](evidence/rq7_reinvestigation_results.json).
 
-Analysis: Every percentage is relative to no position encoding after independent LR tuning. Several leading treatments are mutually unresolved on ranking quality; coverage reveals material trade-offs that recall alone hides.
+Analysis: Selection uses best-epoch validation recall@100, then same-epoch NDCG@100, after each native-500M LR boundary is resolved; the table reports restored-checkpoint full-user metrics. The RoPE comparison is complete and uses the selected seed-42 run plus seed-43/44 confirmations. Plain base-10,000 RoPE trails ALiBi by 0.000847 recall@100 and 0.000703 NDCG@100 on the three-seed means, both inside the approved comparability bands. Forward-only learned rows are resolved, but every forward+reverse row is pending the r4 native-500M surface; superseded combined r1/r3 native artifacts and concat r1/r2 diagnostics are excluded.
 
-Conclusion: ALiBi has the highest displayed ranking metrics, but forward learned and several ALiBi/RoPE combinations are within the declared thresholds. Plain forward or reverse RoPE is unresolved against no encoding, while several mismatched learned/rotary combinations regress materially. Position information helps when encoded compatibly, but the evidence does not isolate a unique ranking-quality winner among the leading treatments.
+Conclusion: Plain forward RoPE is comparable to ALiBi under repeated native-500M evidence; adding ALiBi to RoPE is also inside the same ranking bands. No forward+reverse learned treatment is accepted or rejected from this generated report until the r4 LR surfaces finish.
 
